<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhenia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rheneia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhenia is an uninhabited Greek island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a>, just west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delos">Delos</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polycrates">Polycrates of Samos</a> captured it in the sixth century BCE and dedicated it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a>, binding it to Delos with a chain. After the Athenian purification of Delos in 426 BCE, births and burials were forbidden on the sacred island and graves were moved to Rhenia, which served as its cemetery.</p></div>
